invariant: INV-38
file: tcp_nonblocking_frame.c
catches: tcp_nonblocking_loop_test
reason: ch_record_whole_len answers 0 for a header whose length is above
  2^14 + 256, so a caller waits for a body no peer may send. A caller
  whose buffer is smaller than that length waits until its own timeout,
  where the header alone lets ch_read refuse the record at once. The
  frame rows for the first length past the cap object.

--- old
    if (body_len > RECORD_BODY_MAX) {
        return REC_HDR;
    }
--- new
    if (body_len > RECORD_BODY_MAX) {
        return 0;
    }
